# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Tutorial Hub
# Multi-file onboarding flow with one script per feature area.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_hub
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}

{{BG_DECL}}@label start
{{BG_START}}[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1700]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.28]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.42]
[show lavender center talking]
[wait 200]

Lavender: Welcome to the built-in JVN tutorial pack for this project.
Lavender: Each topic is its own {b}.vns{/b} file under {b}scripts/tutorial/{/b}, similar to Ren'Py-style example packs.
Lavender: The pack now includes fundamentals, advanced systems, and production/release workflow lessons.
Lavender: Every lesson is intentionally long-form so teams can treat these files as living references.

@label topics_page_1
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: Fundamentals page:
> 01. Writing Dialogue and Text Tags -> open_dialogue
> 02. Narration and Pacing -> open_narration
> 03. Expressions and Character Setup -> open_expressions
> 04. Images and Backgrounds -> open_images
> Next: Systems and Animation -> topics_page_2
> Exit tutorial -> end_early

@label topics_page_2
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: Systems and animation page:
> 05. Transitions and Screen FX -> open_transitions
> 06. Audio and Music -> open_audio
> 07. Variables and Conditions -> open_variables
> 08. Character Movement and Easing -> open_movement
> 09. Puppeteer Timeline from VNS -> open_puppeteer
> 10. Choices and Built-in Menus -> open_menus
> 11. Subroutines and Flow Composition -> open_subroutines
> 12. Best Practices Checklist -> open_best_practices
> Next: Production workflow -> topics_page_3
> Back to fundamentals -> topics_page_1
> Exit tutorial -> end_early

@label topics_page_3
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: Production workflow page:
> 13. Camera and Staging -> open_camera
> 14. Localization and Text Keys -> open_localization
> 15. UI Layout and Theme Integration -> open_ui_layout
> 16. Testing and Release Workflow -> open_testing_release
> Jump back to fundamentals -> topics_page_1
> Jump back to systems page -> topics_page_2
> Exit tutorial -> end_early

@label open_dialogue
[goto {{DIALOGUE_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_narration
[goto {{NARRATION_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_expressions
[goto {{EXPRESSIONS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_images
[goto {{IMAGES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_transitions
[goto {{TRANSITIONS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_audio
[goto {{AUDIO_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_variables
[goto {{VARIABLES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_movement
[goto {{MOVEMENT_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_puppeteer
[goto {{PUPPETEER_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_menus
[goto {{MENUS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_subroutines
[goto {{SUBROUTINES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_best_practices
[goto {{BEST_PRACTICES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_camera
[goto {{CAMERA_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_localization
[goto {{LOCALIZATION_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_ui_layout
[goto {{UI_LAYOUT_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_testing_release
[goto {{TESTING_RELEASE_TARGET}}:start]

@label end_early
[show lavender center talking]
[wait 160]
[if tutorial_count > 13]
Lavender: You explored nearly the entire tutorial pack. Great pace.
[elif tutorial_count > 7]
Lavender: Strong progress. You already covered both fundamentals and advanced systems.
[else]
Lavender: Start with one track and revisit the rest as your production needs evolve.
[endif]
Lavender: Open these files directly in the editor and adapt them to your project's own standards.
[end]
